## 3. Decision Rules

### 3.1 When to add Sub-Coordinators
Add a sub-coordinator **only if ALL three** are true:
1. The sub-domain has its own distinct workflow (different tools, different reviewer criteria).
2. Running its phases in parallel with the other sub-domain creates real value.
3. A single Analyst/Executor/Reviewer trio cannot handle both sub-domains efficiently.

If any condition fails → keep a flat pyramid (Coordinator + trio). **Avoid over-engineering.**

### 3.2 When to merge Analyst + Executor
Only merge if the analysis is trivial (< 10% of phase effort). Otherwise keep them separate — clean separation of "know" from "do" improves quality.

### 3.3 When to split Reviewer
Split the Reviewer role **only if** output verification requires fundamentally different skills (e.g., `CodeReviewer` + `UXReviewer` for a fullstack team).

### 3.4 Tool assignment per role
| Role | Typical tools |
|------|---------------|
| Conductor | `agent/runSubagent`, `edit/createFile` (for plan files only), `read/readFile`, `todo` |
| Analyst/Planner | `search/*`, `read/readFile`, `read/viewImage` (if visual), `fetch` (if web research) |
| Executor/Implementer | `edit/*`, `execute/runInTerminal`, `runCommands`, `read/viewImage` (if vision needed), domain-specific |
| Reviewer | `search/*`, `read/readFile`, `problems`, `changes`, `browser` (if UI) |

**Never give the Conductor execution tools** (runInTerminal, runCommands, edit/editFiles beyond plan files). This enforces the MANDATORY rule at the tool level.

