## 6. Anti-patterns to Avoid

- ❌ Generic names (`planning-subagent`, `review-subagent`) across pipelines
- ❌ Giving the Conductor execution tools
- ❌ Skipping the MANDATORY block
- ❌ Creating sub-coordinators for flat problems
- ❌ Merging Analyst into Conductor (Coordinator must NEVER research directly)
- ❌ Omitting the Reviewer role — quality gates are non-negotiable
- ❌ Forgetting `agents:` list in Conductor frontmatter
- ❌ Forgetting the corporate language / palette when the workspace requires it

---

## 7. Output Checklist (before delivering)

- [ ] All agent files created in `.github/agents/` with `.agent.md` extension
- [ ] Conductor contains the MANDATORY block verbatim
- [ ] Conductor references subagents by EXACT name in both `agents:` frontmatter and `<subagent_instructions>`
- [ ] Every subagent has: `description`, `tools`, `model` frontmatter
- [ ] Every subagent states "called by parent **{DomainPrefix}Conductor**"
- [ ] Reviewer's output format includes `Status (APPROVED/NEEDS_REVISION/FAILED)`
- [ ] Stopping rules enumerated (at least 3 pause points)
- [ ] Optional: domain-specific `SKILL.md` created if the team needs shared knowledge
- [ ] Mermaid pyramid presented and approved by user
